SFArmPlatformExpert: start the secondary cores of an Apple SoC

SFAppleBootCPUPMGR was the boot-CPU-only IOPMGR: enableCPUCore() panicked, so the M1 ran
on one efficiency core with cpus=1. It now releases a core from reset the way m1n1 does
(src/smp.c, smp_start_cpu): after checking the core's reset vector register (the first
word of cpu-impl-reg) against the address xnu passes, and writing it where it is not
locked, it sets the core's bit in the CPU-start block of PMGR (+0x4, without which the
core takes no IRQs) and the core's bit in its cluster's start word (+0x8 + 4 * cluster).
The block's offset in /arm-io/pmgr is per SoC, from m1n1's table; only T8103 has been run.

Every case it cannot handle (unknown SoC, a second die, a locked reset vector that is not
xnu's, no reset vector at all) panics with the reason. Power-down still panics.

--- a/src/Kernel/Extensions/SFArmPlatformExpert/SFAppleBootCPUPMGR.cpp
+++ b/src/Kernel/Extensions/SFArmPlatformExpert/SFAppleBootCPUPMGR.cpp
@@ -1,20 +1,64 @@
